From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mio <mio@mio19.uk>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:16:15 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] modules/rootfs: create standard /var symlinks in the image

The generated Mobile-NixOS rootfs image did not contain /var/run or /var/lock, so stage-1 and tmpfiles workarounds were needed. Create the standard symlinks in populateCommands so every boot sees them before early systemd units.
---
 modules/rootfs.nix | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/rootfs.nix b/modules/rootfs.nix
index 0af0c136..6c49de0b 100644
--- a/modules/rootfs.nix
+++ b/modules/rootfs.nix
@@ -49,6 +49,11 @@ in
       in
       ''
         mkdir -p ./nix/store
+        # The generated rootfs must contain the standard /var symlinks before
+        # systemd starts; creating them in stage 1 is too late for early units.
+        mkdir -p ./var
+        ln -sfn /run ./var/run
+        ln -sfn /run/lock ./var/lock
         echo "Copying system closure..."
 
         err=0
